-- title:
--   Canonical X-minus-jumps stopped C2 controlled Gaussian finite predictable gain sum is square integrable
-- statement:
--   For the canonical spectrally negative Levy source X on its original space and filtration, the finite sum of stopped, bounded, source C2 left-limit controlled-derivative gains times its continuous Gaussian residual increments is L2. Stopping-history measurability of the actual derivative is established from the original dividend strategy. The Gaussian Y and pathwise original X decomposition remain hypotheses.
-- source:
--   Uses the remotely Proved joint C2 source stopped derivative predictability and the remotely Proved finite predictable Gaussian stopped L2 theorem applied to a same-space zero-jump Y, transferred via explicit source decomposition.

